<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar output nearing 5.0 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar output nearing 5.0 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's sugar production is nearing its peak with 4.94 million tonnes produced as of March 17 compared with 4.80 million tonnes in the corresponding period last year, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The yield also improved to 102.19 kg of sugar per tonne of cane versus 100.98 kg last week.</p>
<p>&quot;Cane quality was far better than that at the start of the crushing season,&quot; said an industry source. The crushing season started in November and normally ends in May or June.</p>
<p>As of March 17, a total of 48.31 million tonnes of sugar cane had been crushed to produce 2.86 million tonnes of raw sugar and 2.07 million tonnes of white sugar.</p>
<p>The following is the comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period last season (in tonnes unless otherwise specified):</p>
<p>				   March 17, 1997	 March 17,1996</p>
<p>Crushed sugar cane		 48,310,507	    46,366,466</p>
<p>Raw Sugar			     2,866,814	     2,829,728</p>
<p>White and refined sugar	   2,070,107	     2,050,845</p>
<p>Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	   11.62		   12.03</p>
<p>Yield					102.19		  105.26</p>
<p>Molasses				2,072,218	     2,141,051</p>
<p>Yield					 42.89		   46.18</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
